"""
Grafana's `otel-lgtm` stack, to demo the examples' traces and metrics. LGTM is Grafana's name for its observability
stack: Loki for logs, Grafana to see them, Tempo for traces, and Mimir for metrics; the `otel-lgtm` image puts an
OpenTelemetry collector in front of them, with Prometheus for the metrics, all in one container. It isn't part of
Bootable; an example's module takes it as its OTLP collector, a service setting, which `dagger.toml` wires to
`otelStack`.
"""
type OtelLgtm {
  """
  The OTEL stack: Grafana on port 3000, and an OTLP collector on 4318.

  Grafana's LGTM stack, of Loki for logs, Grafana, Tempo for traces, and Prometheus for metrics, behind an
  OpenTelemetry collector, whose OTLP receiver is on 4318, over HTTP. `dagger start` tunnels both ports to
  `localhost`.
  """
  @up
  pub otelStack: Service! {
    container
      .from("docker.io/grafana/otel-lgtm:0.41.0")
      .withExposedPort(3000)
      .withExposedPort(4318)
      .asService
  }
}
